"TOFD uses separate transmitting and receiving angle-beam probes placed on opposite sides of the examination zone. The display records the lateral wave near the top surface, diffracted signals from discontinuity tips, and the back-wall signal. Unlike amplitude-based methods, TOFD relies primarily on arrival time and known probe/component geometry to estimate tip positions.",
"A crack can generate diffraction from its upper and lower extremities. If both tips are resolved and geometry is calibrated, their positions can estimate through-wall height. Probe centre spacing (PCS), refracted angle, material velocity, time-base calibration and probe alignment influence the geometric solution. The signal often appears hyperbolic as the probe pair moves relative to a point diffractor.",
